'''vacation''' (vā-kā′shọn), ''n.'' [< ME. ''vacacion'', ''vacacioun'', < OF. ''vacacion'', ''vacation'', F. ''vacation'' = Pr. ''vaccatio'' = Sp. ''vacacion'' = Pg. ''vacação'' = It. ''vacazione'', < L. ''vacatio(n-)'', leisure, < ''vacare'', pp. ''vacatus'', be empty, free, or unoccupied: see ''vacate''.] '''1.''' The act of vacating. {{smaller|Specifically—(''a'') The act of leaving without an occupant: as, the ''vacation'' of an office. (''b'') The act of making void, vacant, or of}}
